00:40:55.730 --> 00:41:18.470
<v Ira  Glass>Brian Reed. He's the senior producer of our program and the host of the podcast S-Town, which is about another small town, that one in Alabama. Coming up, we return to the lower 48, to a high school in Maryland, and an incident that even got the president's attention. That's in a minute from Chicago Public Radio, when our program continues.
<v Ira  Glass>布莱恩·里德。他是我们节目的高级制片人，也是播客《S-Town》的主持人，该播客是关于另一个小镇的，那个小镇在阿拉巴马州。接下来，我们将回到美国本土，回到马里兰州的一所高中，以及一起甚至引起总统注意的事件。一分钟后，来自芝加哥公共电台，当我们的节目继续时。

00:41:18.470 --> 00:41:56.140
<v Ira       Glass>This American Life, from Ira Glass. Today's program, "Fear and Loathing in Homer and Rockville." We have two stories of places where people got really scared about immigrants, where immigration did not seem to be the main thing going on. We've arrived at Act Two of our program. Act Two, Loathing. So the first half of our program was about a community that was worried about what might happen, theoretically, if undocumented immigrants arrived. This next story happens in a place where they actually already have arrived-- Rockville, Maryland, a suburb of Washington, D.C., where this winter, something actually did happen. And the whole community had to deal with it. Zoe Chace explains.
<v Ira       Glass>《美国生活》，来自艾拉·格拉斯（Ira Glass）。今天的节目，“荷马和罗克维尔的恐惧与厌恶”。我们有两个关于人们对移民感到非常害怕的地方的故事，那里的移民问题似乎根本不是当地发生的主要事情。我们已经进入了节目的第二幕。第二幕，厌恶。所以我们节目的前半部分是关于一个社区担心如果无证移民到达会发生什么（理论上）。接下来的这个故事发生在他们实际上已经到达的地方——马里兰州的罗克维尔，华盛顿特区的一个郊区，今年冬天，真的发生了一些事情。整个社区都不得不处理它。佐伊·查斯（Zoe Chace）来解释。

00:41:56.140 --> 00:42:09.560
<v Zoe Chace>Here's the thing that happened. A freshman girl in the local high school said she was raped by two undocumented immigrant students. She said it happened at 9:00 on a Thursday morning, in the boys' bathroom at the school.
<v Zoe Chace>发生的事情是这样的。当地高中的一名新生女生说，她被两名无证移民学生强奸了。她说这发生在周四早上9点，在学校的男生洗手间。

00:42:09.560 --> 00:42:21.010
<v Zoe Chace>The boys were new students. They'd crossed the border separately from El Salvador and Guatemala. Jose was 17. Henry was 18. The girl was 14. They were all ninth graders, though.
<v Zoe Chace>这两个男孩是新生。他们分别从萨尔瓦多和危地马拉越过边境。何塞（Jose）17岁。亨利（Henry）18岁。女生14岁。虽然他们都是九年级的学生。

00:42:21.010 --> 00:42:31.440
<v Zoe Chace>The superintendent of schools, Jack Smith-- was the person who'd have to manage the situation. The police, the parents, the students, the press. I talked to him while he was dealing with all that, back in March.
<v Zoe Chace>学校校长杰克·史密斯（Jack Smith）——是不得不管理这种情况的人。警方、家长、学生、媒体。三月份的时候，我在他处理这些事情时采访了他。

00:42:31.440 --> 00:42:46.320
<v Jack Smith>I couldn't understand how it could have happened in a busy high school with 1,500 students and a large staff. Felt sick at my stomach. So I was confused as to what could have happened.
<v Jack Smith>我无法理解这怎么会在一所拥有1500名学生和大量教职员工的繁忙高中发生。我感到恶心。所以我很困惑到底发生了什么。

00:42:46.320 --> 00:42:52.480
<v Zoe Chace>In less than 24 hours, TV trucks were showing up at the school. Local television and radio, mostly.
<v Zoe Chace>不到24小时，电视转播车就出现在学校了。主要是当地电视和电台。

