<v Tucker Carlson>Well, good evening, and welcome to Tucker Carlson Tonight. Just days ago, a hideous crime was allegedly committed in the Washington, D.C. suburb of Rockville, Maryland.
<v Tucker Carlson>晚上好，欢迎收看《塔克·卡尔森今晚秀》（Tucker Carlson Tonight）。就在几天前，华盛顿特区郊区马里兰州罗克维尔发生了一起令人发指的罪行。

00:43:22.830 --> 00:43:26.560
<v Zoe Chace>Fox News covered the case in Rockville every day, the Tucker Carlson show in particular.
<v Zoe Chace>福克斯新闻每天都在报道罗克维尔的案件，特别是塔克·卡尔森的节目。

00:43:26.560 --> 00:43:44.110
<v Tucker Carlson>Sanchez is 18 years old and in this country illegally. But instead of being deported back to his country of origin, he was instead placed in the ninth grade and educated at taxpayer expense. This is insanity, of course. It's a sign of a sick civilization at war with itself.
<v Tucker Carlson>桑切斯（Sanchez）18岁，在这个国家非法居留。但他没有被驱逐回原籍国，而是被安排在九年级，并由纳税人出钱接受教育。这当然是疯狂的。这是一个正在自我战争的病态文明的标志。

00:43:44.110 --> 00:43:58.460
<v Zoe Chace>That was the general tone of the coverage on Fox. This rape allegation is a great example of how terrible our immigration policies are. They turned the case into a referendum. You didn't see much coverage of the allegation on other major news networks.
<v Zoe Chace>这就是福克斯报道的基调。这起强奸指控是我们的移民政策有多糟糕的一个很好的例子。他们把这个案件变成了一次公投。你在其他主要新闻网络上没看到多少关于该指控的报道。

00:43:58.460 --> 00:44:17.750
<v Zoe Chace>In the week after, it was mentioned only twice on CNN, once in The New York Times. Local D.C. TV and local papers, like The Washington Post and The Washington Times-- they stayed on it. But Fox News and other online conservative media, they did not skip a day that week. The school superintendent Jack Smith, watched the story take off.
<v Zoe Chace>在一周之后，它只在CNN上提到过两次，在《纽约时报》上提到过一次。当地的华盛顿特区电视台和当地报纸，如《华盛顿邮报》和《华盛顿时报》——他们一直关注它。但福克斯新闻和其他在线保守派媒体，那一周一天都没落下。学校校长杰克·史密斯，看着这个故事起飞。

00:44:17.750 --> 00:44:46.410
<v Jack Smith>We just watched it grow over Friday, Friday night, Saturday, thinking, you know, how do we separate this-- the horrific situation-- from the immigration debate? And knowing that we weren't going to be able to. I mean, you couldn't have lived through the last 18 months in the United States and not have been inundated with the perspectives on those things.
<v Jack Smith>我们只是看着它在周五、周五晚上、周六增长，思考着，你知道，我们怎么才能把这——那种可怕的情况——从移民辩论中分离出来？并且知道我们做不到。我的意思是，你不可能在过去18个月里生活在美国，却没有被那些观点所淹没。

00:44:46.410 --> 00:44:57.770
<v Zoe Chace>Jack Smith was named in the coverage as the guy responsible for the schools. And voicemails and emails started pouring into the school district from all over the country with a clear message for him.
<v Zoe Chace>杰克·史密斯在报道中被点名为负责学校的人。来自全国各地的语音信箱和邮件开始涌入学校区，向他传达了一个明确的信息。

00:44:57.770 --> 00:45:00.450
<v Voicemail  Recording>01:00 AM.
<v Voicemail  Recording>凌晨1点。

00:45:00.450 --> 00:45:23.960
<v Male Caller To Voicemail>Yes, hello, to the wonderful school board that hired a Jack Smith. I'd like to say I'm the father of three young girls that were not raped by illegal aliens. Fire this man. And hopefully all the rest of you nitwits at that school board will be fired next for letting illegal aliens in.
